{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2165-10-26 23:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I understand you’ve been having some chest pressure and epigastric discomfort?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2165-10-26 23:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been coming and going for a few days. It feels like pressure right here in the middle, under my breastbone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2165-10-26 23:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned in the ER that you’ve had this before. Was it helped by any medication?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2165-10-26 23:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Prilosec helped last time. But I ran out a week ago — I couldn’t afford to refill it. The symptoms started again about four days after I stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2165-10-26 23:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ve reviewed your history — you’ve had heart issues before, including bypass surgery. But this sounds a lot like heartburn, especially since it improved with Prilosec previously."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried it was my heart again. I’ve been so anxious lately — with money problems and my tenant not paying rent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Your EKG was unchanged from your baseline, and we checked your cardiac enzymes three times — all negative. That rules out a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. But why did my heart race earlier today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had a brief episode of tachycardia this morning. Your blood pressure was low — 98 systolic — so we held your morning beta-blocker. Once we gave it again, your heart rate settled down. It’s likely tied to anxiety and the medication timing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so stressed. I didn’t know what else to do — that’s why I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Coming in was the right choice. We want to make sure your symptoms aren’t heart-related. The chest X-ray was clear — no heart failure or lung issues. Your echo showed your heart is pumping well, though there’s mild mitral valve leakage, which we’ve seen before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stress test? I remember doing one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the stress test showed normal blood flow to your heart. You stopped early because your blood pressure dropped, but you didn’t have chest pain or ECG changes. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s really not my heart this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2165-10-27 00:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, the testing confirms it’s not a cardiac event. Your symptoms are most likely from acid reflux — especially since they returned when you stopped Prilosec."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to discharge you today. We’ve restarted Prilosec and prescribed the prescription-strength version — it’s covered by your insurance. We’re also switching your Toprol to the extended-release form for smoother blood pressure control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And the social worker mentioned something about a report?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, she’s filing a report regarding possible financial exploitation by your tenant. She’ll connect you with support services."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. I’ve felt so alone with all this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re not alone. Keep taking your medications as prescribed. If you have chest pain, shortness of breath, jaw or arm pain, or nausea, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll follow up with my primary doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please schedule a visit within the next week. We’ll send them a summary. You’re stable now — no chest pressure, and your vitals are good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better knowing it’s not my heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself — both physically and emotionally. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications. You should be ready to go home in about 20 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready. I just hope I can get some relief now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2165-10-27 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You should. With the Prilosec back on track and some support in place, things should improve. Take it one step at a time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2165-10-26 23:46:00",
    "admission_end": "2165-10-27 19:23:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 70-year-old woman with a history of coronary artery disease, prior CABG, and anxiety presented with recurrent epigastric and substernal pressure that began after she stopped taking Prilosec due to financial constraints. She reported increased anxiety and social stressors, including concerns about financial exploitation by her tenant. Initial evaluation in the ED showed stable vital signs, no ischemic EKG changes, and negative cardiac enzymes across three tests. A chest X-ray revealed no acute findings, and an echocardiogram showed normal ejection fraction with mild mitral regurgitation. A stress test demonstrated normal myocardial perfusion without ischemic changes. Her symptoms were attributed to gastroesophageal reflux, and she was restarted on Prilosec with a prescription covered by insurance. Her Toprol was switched to the extended-release formulation. Social work evaluated her situation and initiated a report for possible elder financial abuse. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with her primary care provider and to return if cardiac symptoms developed.",
    "problems": [
      "Heartburn",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status"
    ]
  }
}
